# Cloudflare Pages response headers (https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/headers/).
# The build adds its own rules after these (Nitro's cloudflare-pages-static preset: `/_nuxt/*` and
# `/_fonts/*` immutable for a year, their names carry a hash). Hosting notes: docs/HOSTING.md.

# Every response. Pages already sends X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff and
# Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin; these add the rest.
# - The camera for the barcode scanner (#92), for Libellus itself only; off: what the app never
#   asks for. (Vibration is not a policy feature, nothing to allow.)
# - Never framed: everything personal sits behind the sign-in.
# - The Content-Security-Policy only reports for now (in the browser console): what the app
#   loads, from where. Supabase (API, functions, realtime), Apple and Open Library (search,
#   covers, their thumbhash read with CORS), the owner's shelf (`books.fabkho.dev`, Regal's
#   textures as blobs), the barcode decoder (WebAssembly), Cloudflare Web Analytics (the
#   beacon Pages adds to the HTML, docs/HOSTING.md). Covers come from any https host (an
#   imported Book keeps its own). 'unsafe-inline' for scripts: the theme boot script, the
#   import map and Nuxt's runtime config are inline, and two of them change with every build.
/*
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(self), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=(), usb=(), browsing-topics=()
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Content-Security-Policy-Report-Only: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' 'wasm-unsafe-eval' https://static.cloudflareinsights.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data: blob: https:; font-src 'self' data:; connect-src 'self' https://*.supabase.co wss://*.supabase.co https://books.fabkho.dev https://itunes.apple.com https://openlibrary.org https://covers.openlibrary.org https://*.mzstatic.com https://cloudflareinsights.com; media-src 'self' blob:; worker-src 'self' blob:; manifest-src 'self'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'

# The service worker, the script it imports and the manifest have fixed names: always asked
# again, so a new deploy reaches installed apps on their next start.
/sw.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/sw-sync.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/manifest.webmanifest
  Cache-Control: no-cache

# The Pages address of production (libellus-3q1.pages.dev) stays reachable, without a
# redirect, but out of search results: libellus.fabkho.dev is the one address. Preview and
# branch addresses (<id>.libellus-3q1.pages.dev) get noindex from Pages already.
https://:project.pages.dev/*
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex
